Leaving intercept mode: clear the DBus targets' state

The DBus target drops a button event that matches the state it last saw
(is_duplicate_event). A button pressed while the composite device
intercepts (Always) goes to the DBus target; if the device goes back to
Pass or None before the button is released, the release goes to the other
targets, so the DBus target keeps the button "pressed" and drops every
later press of it. clear_state() exists on the DBus target (it releases
held buttons, stick directions and triggers) but is called only for the
other targets.

HinterOS hit this with Guide in Pass mode: the press switches to Always and
reaches the session daemon; a long press makes the daemon set Pass while
Guide is still held (to tap Guide for Steam), the release goes to the
gamepad, and the next Guide presses never reach D-Bus until a release
happens while intercepting. Same in v0.83.0 and master (2026-10).
Upstream: https://github.com/ShadowBlip/InputPlumber
(src/input/composite_device/mod.rs, fn set_intercept_mode).

--- a/src/input/composite_device/mod.rs
+++ b/src/input/composite_device/mod.rs
@@ -1239,8 +1239,12 @@
         }
         self.intercept_mode = mode;
 
-        // Nothing else is required when turning off input interception.
+        // When turning off input interception, release whatever the DBus targets
+        // still hold: a button pressed while intercepting and released after the
+        // switch went to the other targets, and the DBus target would otherwise
+        // drop its next press as a duplicate.
         if mode == InterceptMode::None || mode == InterceptMode::Pass {
+            self.targets.clear_dbus_state().await;
             return;
         }
 
--- a/src/input/composite_device/targets.rs
+++ b/src/input/composite_device/targets.rs
